L725: #### Significant Effects of Time
L726: Mean scores and ratings are reported with the Standard Deviation (SD). Effect sizes for significant results are reported using Cohen’s D (d).
L727: #### Choice Reaction Time (CRT)
L728: A significant effect of time was found for CRT accuracy (F(2,76) = 4.73, p = 0.012), with better performance seen pre- and immediately post-exercise compared to 80 min post-exercise (p = 0.18, d = 0.28 and p = 0.19, d = 0.28 respectively).
L729: #### Rapid Visual Information Processing (RVIP)
L730: A significant effect of time was found for RVIP correct RT (F(2,76) = 5.48, p = 0.006), with faster reaction time (RT) seen immediately post-exercise compared to pre-exercise (p = 0.014, d = 0.30).
L731: #### Delayed Word Recall
L732: A significant effect of time was found for Delayed Word Recall correct responses (F(2,76) = 8.79,
L733: p < 0.0001), with better performance seen immediately post-exercise compared to pre-exercise and
L734: 80 min post-exercise (p = 0.012, d = 0.35 and p = 0.001, d = 0.49 respectively).
L735: #### Word Recognition
L736: A significant effect of time was found for Word Recognition RT (F(2,76) = 6.10, p = 0.004), with faster RT seen pre-exercise compared to immediately post-exercise and 80 min post-exercise (p = 0.023, d = 0.34 and p = 0.013, d = 0.37 respectively).
L737: #### Picture Recognition
L738: A significant effect of time was found for Picture Recognition reaction time (F(2,76) = 7.59, p = 0.001), with faster RT seen at 80 min exercise compared to pre-exercise (p = 0.002, d = 0.25).
L739: #### Alertness
L740: A significant effect of time was found for ratings of alertness (F(2,78) = 8.17, p = 0.002), which were higher immediately post-exercise compared to pre-exercise (p = 0.020, d = 0.40) but lower
L741: 80 min post-exercise compared to immediately post-exercise (p = 0.001, d = 0.48).
L742: #### Calmness
L743: A significant effect of time was found for ratings of calmness (F(2,78) = 49.37, p < 0.0001). Ratings were significantly lower immediately post-exercise compared to pre-exercise (p < 0.0001,
L744: d = 0.71) but higher at 80 min post-exercise compared to pre−exercise (p < 0.0001, d = 0.77) and immediately post-exercise (p < 0.0001, d = 1.25).
L745: #### Felt Arousal Scale (FAS)
L746: A significant effect of time was found for ratings of arousal (F(5,195) = 29.28, p < 0.0001). Arousal ratings increased at every time point during exercise compared to pre-exercise (10 min, d = 32; 20 min, d = 0.46; 30 min, d = 0.51; all p < 0.0001), but fell significantly by 50 min post exercise (p < 0.0001,
L747: d = 0.90).
L748: #### Rating of Perceived Exertion (RPE)
L749: There was a significant effect of time for RPE (F(2,78) = 4.90, p = 0.033), which significantly increased at each time point during the exercise period 10–20 min, d = 0.60; 20–30 min, d = 0.24;
L750: 10–30 min, d = 0.81; all p < 0.0001).
L751: #### Respiratory Exchange Rate (RER)
L752: There was a significant effect of time for RER (F(2,66) = 138.82, p < 0.0001), which significantly decreased at each time point during the exercise period (9–19 min, d = 0.91; 19–29 min, d = 0.59;
L753: 9–29 min, d = 1.65; all p < 0.0001).
L754: #### Energy Expenditure (EE)
L755: There was a significant effect of time for EE (F(2,66) = 11.70, p < 0.0001) which was significantly higher during minute 29 than during minutes 9 (p < 0.0001, d = 0.19) and 19 (p = 0.002, d = 0.10) of the exercise period.
L756: #### Fat Oxidation
L757: There was a significant effect of time for fat oxidation (F(2,68) = 164.43, p < 0.0001), which significantly increased at each time point during the exercise period (9–19 min, d = 0.87; 19–29 min,
L758: d = 0.56; 9–29 min, d = 1.54; all p < 0.0001).
L759: #### Carbohydrate (CHO) Oxidation
L760: There was a significant effect of time for CHO oxidation (F(2,68) = 60.43, p < 0.0001), which significantly decreased at each time point during the exercise period (9–19 min, d = 0.39; 19–29 min,
L761: d = 0.20; 9–29 min, d = 0.61; all p < 0.0001).
